id: pm-mkzw1x
title: "Merge-fence scope ambiguity: extension-contributed item folders make default validation disagree with the no-extensions CI baseline"
description: "Default extension-aware pm validate and pm merge install include item types contributed by active project extensions, while the repository merge-safety CI deliberately runs both commands with --no-extensions. The same committed .gitattributes can therefore be reported stale locally and over-specified in CI. Define a stable project-schema versus optional-runtime-extension fence contract, surface the selected scope in diagnostics, and ensure one documented command produces the committed baseline without contradictory remediation."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[6]: ci,extensions,merge,multi-agent,ux,validation
created_at: "2026-07-27T01:53:33.846Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T01:53:33.846Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The committed fence has one explicit reproducible schema scope shared by CI and operator guidance; default validation does not recommend a change that the required CI gate reverses; diagnostics name whether core project schema or active extension schema was audited; tests cover tracked project profiles and optional runtime-only profiles without weakening custom item merge protection
parent: pm-g5sx
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: pm validate and pm merge install with active project extensions versus --no-extensions CI
expected_result: Local diagnostics and CI agree on the committed semantic merge-fence contract.
actual_result: Extension-aware local validation requested ten optional profile folder patterns that the no-extensions CI then removed and rejected.
component: merge-fence-governance
